Vita (--vita-fast-search=off|on|verify): process searches (fpcLyIt_AllJudge: fpcM_Search,
fpcEx_Search, fpcM_SearchByName, fpcEx_SearchByID) and actor queue searches (fopAcIt_Judge:
fopAcM_SearchByID, fopAcM_SearchByName, fopAcM_Search) with the same judge calls in the same order.
The original chases every layer's node lists (node, next node, tag data) for each search; the fast
path keeps one walk's tags and tag data in arrays and hands the judge the data from there while no
node list anywhere changed (twv_cls_generation, patches/dusklight/0031). The count is read after
every judge call: once a judge changed a list, the search goes on exactly as the original loop
would from that point (the next node it had already read, then live links, the layer's remaining
lists, the remaining layers). verify runs the original walk for the game (judges may have side
effects, so they run once) and compares the kept arrays with a fresh walk. Off (0) unless the Vita
entry selects it; the counts go to platform/vita/runtime/fast_actors.cpp.

